  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Chain stitch works by always inserting the needle back through the previous loop, so each new loop holds the one before it open. The chain builds quickly once the rhythm is established and follows curves with ease because each individual loop is short.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What you need",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Thread",
              "value": "Stranded cotton, 3 to 4 strands for a bold line"
            },
            {
              "label": "Fabric",
              "value": "Cotton or linen"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needle",
              "value": "Embroidery needle size 9"
            },
            {
              "label": "Hoop",
              "value": "15 cm embroidery hoop"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Working a practice line",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Bring the needle up at point A. Hold the thread in a loop below the line with your thumb.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Insert the needle back at A and bring it up one stitch-length ahead at B, passing through the loop. Pull through gently until the loop forms a rounded oval.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "For the next chain: hold the thread in a new loop, insert at B (inside the previous loop), bring up at C. Continue along the line.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "To finish the last loop, make one small tacking stitch over its tip rather than beginning a new chain.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Common mistakes",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "intro": "Two common problems.",
          "items": [
            {
              "fix": "Pull each loop to the same gentle tension before forming the next one. Consistent finger pressure is the main control.",
              "cause": "The thread is pulled to different tensions on each stitch.",
              "symptom": "Loops are uneven sizes"
            },
            {
              "fix": "Aim for loops roughly 4 to 6 mm long.",
              "cause": "Stitch length is too short, so the loops crowd together.",
              "symptom": "The chain looks like a series of bumps"
            }
          ],
          "heading": "When chain stitch goes wrong"
        }
      },
